: 0, "impression_count": 2074, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "Gilead Sciences agreed to pay $45 million to settle allegations of paying kickbacks that improperly influenced prescriptions paid for by the Texas Medicaid program https://t.co/A96qWbZ5s6", "url": "https://x.com/statnews/status/2113409287116517804"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["13_2113382392706596864"]}, "author_id": "860158302", "created_at": "2026-10-22T21:30:10.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113382427745792495"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "In the late 19th century, Karl Weierstrass invented a fractal-like function that was decried as nothing less than a “deplorable evil.” In time, it would transform the foundations of mathematics.", "display_url": "quantamagazine.org/the-jagged-mon…", "end": 269, "expanded_url": "https://www.quantamagazine.org/the-jagged-monstrous-function-that-broke-calculus-20250123/", "images": [{"height": 630, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113382473795010561/m8HbyI0c?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1200}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113382473795010561/m8HbyI0c?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 246, "status": 200, "title": "The Jagged, Monstrous Function That Broke Calculus | Quanta Magazine", "unwound_url": "https://www.quantamagazine.org/the-jagged-monstrous-function-that-broke-calculus-20250123/", "url": "https://t.co/tMXyKuJIrC"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/qTl2b8sjbr", "end": 293, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/QuantaMagazine/status/2113382427745792495/video/1", "media_key": "13_2113382392706596864", "start": 270, "url": "https://t.co/qTl2b8sjbr"}]}, "id": "2113382427745792495", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 119, "impression_count": 16333, "like_count": 303, "quote_count": 6, "reply_count": 11, "retweet_count": 45}, "text": "This is the Weierstrass function, a “monster” that is continuous everywhere but differentiable nowhere. First published in 1872, it prompted scrutiny of assumptions in calculus. Similar functions are used to study random motion and analyze risk. https://t.co/tMXyKuJIrC https://t.co/qTl2b8sjbr", "url": "https://x.com/QuantaMagazine/status/2113382427745792495"}, {"author_id": "860158302", "created_at": "2026-10-22T21:27:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113381635303387146"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "C.H. Waddington’s powerful image of embryonic stem cells specializing on a rolling landscape has captivated biologists since the 1950s. Experimental data is finally confirming, and complicating, his visionary ideas.", "display_url": "quantamagazine.org/how-does-life-…", "end": 277, "expanded_url": "https://www.quantamagazine.org/how-does-life-unfold-a-landscape-metaphor-comes-into-its-own-20261009/", "images": [{"height": 630, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2112584252185358336/xOGqFy3a?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1200}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2112584252185358336/xOGqFy3a?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 254, "status": 200, "title": "How Does Life Unfold? A Landscape Metaphor Comes Into Its Own. | Quanta Magazine", "unwound_url": "https://www.quantamagazine.org/how-does-life-unfold-a-landscape-metaphor-comes-into-its-own-20261009/", "url": "https://t.co/MjiZa14iSq"}]}, "id": "2113381635303387146", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 87, "impression_count": 12772, "like_count": 184, "quote_count": 2, "reply_count": 4, "retweet_count": 31}, "text": "New analysis reveals that development is not a mere readout of a genetic program, but rather a dynamic process in which communities of cells build themselves, and the very landscape they navigate, by mutual negotiation and interaction, into an organism.\nhttps://t.co/MjiZa14iSq", "url": "https://x.com/QuantaMagazine/status/2113381635303387146"}, {"author_id": "860158302", "created_at": "2026-10-22T21:20:04.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113379887331385658"], "enti